{"title":"Topicwise Test-2 Part Syllabus GATE 2025 EE Electric Circuits-2","fileName":"073_Topicwise Test-2 Part Syllabus GATE 2025 EE Electric Circuits-2.html","branch":"ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING","series":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series Electrical Engineering","provider":"MADE EASY","duration":2700,"questions":[{"qnum":1,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>For the circuit shown below:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/2f75610eedb19f152e2b0adbdf4c76561fb1daef.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>the switch is moved to position 2 at t = 0, the current <img src=\"/media/0c2afa49b6302445785ebdb6104cffd250714709.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> msec is _______ A.</p>\n<p> </p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.5","high":"0.5"},"solution":"<p>0.50 (0.48 - 0.52)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/c19d91af678f8a141becd74f31db8500e5cbb66f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":2,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>For the circuit shown,</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/c9ec8f9b010105c64030216a740dbcebdefc6a7b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>If the power dissipated in the load resistance is 100 W and the network <em>N</em> is represented in terms of h-parameters as <em>h</em><sub>11</sub> = <em>h</em><sub>22</sub> = 1 and <em>h</em><sub>12</sub> = 2, <em>h</em><sub>21</sub> = –2 then the value of source voltage <em>V<sub>s</sub></em> is _____ V.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"50","high":"50"},"solution":"<p>50</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/7f40f10e67aad91b046651e49f4c21b39d3b5d0c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":3,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,D","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider the following circuit:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/9327000a37df098a639a1dcd8f08bb57a9f5ba93.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>Which of the following statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p><img src=\"/media/b1213b26a93860b18ae74015c145102256c65450.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p><img src=\"/media/c762cd7b65b38851c55ac6db78b5ffacd3d88f7d.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> The network is symmetrical</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> The network is reciprocal</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a, d)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/847268982d514150fb8e605f1f7b4e31fbefb3f4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/69bad66079885ed99d202b90aff9a5bb1033b24a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":4,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A series RLC circuit is excited by a variable frequency sinusoidal voltage source having an rms value of 2 V. The maximum rms current in the circuit is found to be 10 mA at a frequency of 10 kHz. At frequencies between 9.6 kHz and 10.4 kHz, the magnitude of the current is to be at least 7.07 mA. The value of L (inductor) is ______ mH. (upto nearest integer).</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"40","high":"40"},"solution":"<p>40 (38 - 42)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/a42516710957c190b88d6910ead2fcaea3c0ae0f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":5,"type":"NAT","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider the circuit shown below:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/bccd75384c3782cb2f2b2b5f206c93e50698a2aa.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>If the switch is closed at <em>t</em> = 0 sec and all components are ideal and capacitors are initially uncharged, the energy (in Joules) transferred from dc source until steady state condition is reached will be _______ J.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"800","high":"800"},"solution":"<p>800 (799 - 801)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/2d8b70286da255f147b50383512eac124a804880.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/f7b2ee0276b0339423819507f4c44a6a8026e3c9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":6,"type":"NAT","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider the circuit shown below. The resonant frequency of the circuit will be equal to _____ rad/sec. (Answer upto two decimal places)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/215e1f7abaec73230caa1f32863251069df4ffab.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.559","high":"0.559"},"solution":"<p>0.559 (0.540 - 0.580)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/345a7906a5f4bb88076a59c01e49a86d34a88e6f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":7,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,C","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider the circuit shown below:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/4d0ed2cded8e4c5dd2492ff0aaf2bc25530cd7e4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>Which of the following statements about the circuit is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p><em>V</em><sub>0</sub> = 4 V, if terminal ‘<em>ab</em>’ is open circuited.</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>Thevenin’s voltage across ab is <em>V</em><sub>Th</sub> = 28 V.</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>Thevenin’s equivalent resistance across <em>ab</em> is <em>R</em><sub>Th</sub> = 11 Ω.</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> Power dissipated in the 2 Ω load resistor is 9.3 W.</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a, c)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/834cd85cfe1eaa6f1c5b7156301f1e0de3d40d7b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/23057e8054962995f4d5d80e69b9d774f0c51707.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":8,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>In an AC circuit, the following quantities are known to us:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/d9f96f44aef9aed53be4a03acd7705949472fa53.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>The total impedance of the circuit will be</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 64 – <em>j</em>48 Ω</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 51.20 – <em>j</em>38.39 Ω</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 51.20 + <em>j</em>38.39 Ω</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 64 + <em>j</em>48 Ω</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/47d8ce7492cd68e344cc17b59488e32858fd3c26.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":9,"type":"NAT","correct":"A","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A 0.2 H inductor carries an AC current of magnitude 0.5 A at 60 Hz. A capacitor is to be connected in parallel with the inductor such that it reduces the magnitude of the current in the inductor to 0.3 A. Assuming that the total current supplied to the network does not change after adding the capacitor, the value of capacitance required will be _______ μF.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"93.9","high":"93.9"},"solution":"<p>93.9 (93.5 - 94.5)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/773934b4a0f43b0f8624100c7d897e8d3454c771.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":10,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>For the circuit showing the figure below, the T-parameter matrix is given by <img src=\"/media/547c6ca62d9f7069ae3a56ef3c7e7e765ff5c138.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/6e895c260143837ac249fdb49d888d86a74db645.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>If the 2 Ω resistor is replaced by 10 Ω resistor, then the new <em>T</em>-parameter matrix [<em>T<sub>B</sub></em>] is equal to</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p><img src=\"/media/4f24d95302540fc1db90ad557f7421a06d714e8b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p><img src=\"/media/a3792525e8bec5f960464a1bb2ce53585d13b182.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p><img src=\"/media/f204093adcd30a753548b856b8399b24b368332f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p><img src=\"/media/b232d73bc9bc08fdd746e2cc291e720a71110f75.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/196d4eb7424aa307502f29102c855e31ff739a0b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":11,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>For the circuit shown below :</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/493ff69bf826a5f48b64e64b527cddd2067f6581.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>voltage <em>V</em><sub>2</sub> is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 35.09 V</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 15.09 V</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 25.09 V</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 45.09 V</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/de3af9fd762cfb68cbb5bd484d2523d3e4367543.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":12,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>In the circuit shown below switch S is closed at (<em>t</em> = 0) the current <img src=\"/media/1717efa49d182ea66b514030eafa5119d4af7ab6.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> through the capacitor at <em>t</em> = 0<sup>+</sup> is</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/a1a6464de36a1d2aa098d236119f2acd1cc79495.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 4 A</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 5 A</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 6 A</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 8 A</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/f136d8f3886c71eea8ab1ac040ca1fde1443cc1a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":13,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>The circuit shown in the given figure is in steady state with switch ‘<em>S</em>’ open,</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/95904ab525e83429d0d104b8bc4d4ac725383943.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>If switch ‘<em>S</em>’ is closed at <em>t</em> = 0, then current <img src=\"/media/75393a3288d7dd08a4d062004d68e823658453b6.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> will be</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> a decreasing exponential</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> an increasing exponential</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> oscillatory</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> constant</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/e2c38b861bb59851b304153aac5531c7990d52ed.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":14,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Consider a DC current source connected to a parallel R-L circuit. When the steady state reaches, the ratio of energy stored in the inductor to the energy supplied by the current source is equal to</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 0.367</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 0.5</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 0.632</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 1</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/ef49a0fa98bb7000723e36e80655b25030071b16.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/2c9bcabc751c67d4f27f9d796eee1f5548d3df1f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":15,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>For the circuit shown below,</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/33c6e91fa85c55928ef846f3ef87ed3300d81945.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>If <img src=\"/media/3189422f560cf8a7c3da995e72bdbbc000edf531.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> then the minimum value of the stored energy is _______ J.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"54","high":"54"},"solution":"<p>54 (53 - 55)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/cdc3a402dcc646821098a5c42dda93bd606ce182.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":16,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>For the circuit shown below:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/8fd6cd920ab1939242e2ac77a4ae679580c634c7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>the Y-parameter <em>y</em><sub>22</sub> is ________ S.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.5","high":"0.5"},"solution":"<p>0.50</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/87a61b3b21c26e268d715796c4dad229438f1760.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":17,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>In the circuit shown below, <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> was closed and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> was open for a very long time. At t = 0, <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> is opened and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> is closed. The voltage across the capacitor, in volts at <em>t</em> = 5 μs is ________ . (Answer upto two decimal places)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/5acdb571e91b0c079b41e44f8a9de31470d0db62.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"1.52","high":"1.52"},"solution":"<p>1.52 (1.50 - 1.54)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/20e5c18e1dec6c2753075b745cc09ea4081331d4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/e88383f7378fb09b25854f3c7555cd585604fe39.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"}],"questionCount":17,"parsedAt":"2026-11-10T19:39:11.910Z"}